# E2E run artifacts (NDJSON logs, captured stdout/stderr, scratch fixtures) — every
# run is reproducible from the scenario script; artifacts are evidence, not source.
/scripts/e2e/artifacts/

# Proposed future exclusions for the extern/builtin census shards (bead
# fln-census-out-of-git-2ya9). The paths remain tracked: this block has no effect
# unless Jeffrey explicitly authorizes removal in a later change.
#
# 231.7 MB of the ~232 MB governed contract surface lives in these four files, and
# they are derived, not authored: gen_extern_census.sh walks a Reference binary
# pin-verified against SUITE.lock, and every projection is deterministic ("derived,
# never remembered"). What makes them checkable is committed and tiny — the
# publication envelope in contracts/EXTERN_BUILTIN_ENVIRONMENT.txt, and the exact
# bytes=/content-root=/identity= pins per shard in contracts/CONTRACT_HANDOFF.txt.
#
# They are still required outputs: structure-guard reads their bytes and the
# handoff root binds them. A future clean checkout would materialise them before
# running the gate with
#   scripts/extract/census_materialize.sh
# which regenerates from the pin and refuses anything whose bytes disagree with the
# committed publication envelope and CONTRACT_HANDOFF.txt lengths.
/contracts/builtin_environment.tsv
/contracts/builtin_environment.001.tsv
/contracts/builtin_environment.002.tsv
/contracts/builtin_partition.tsv

# Skill-loop / repo-janitor scratch
.skill-loop-progress.md
.skill-loop-progress-*.md

# br doctor per-run artifacts
.doctor/
